Input: {"question": "Who is Stephen Ralph Cartwright's spouse?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 99, "text": "\"The Forgotten Union: Unveiling the Hidden Marriage of Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 101, "end": 247, "text": "In the midst of the 19th century, amidst the grandeur of British aristocracy, a clandestine marriage took place, shrouded in secrecy and whispers."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 248, "end": 435, "text": "The union between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Lady Fanny Hay, though seemingly improbable, was a reality that would remain hidden from the prying eyes of society for generations to come."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 436, "end": 684, "text": "This narrative delves into the lives of these two enigmatic figures, unraveling the threads of evidence that weave together to form a tapestry of proof, substantiating the claim that Stephen Ralph Cartwright was, in fact, married to Lady Fanny Hay."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 685, "end": 717, "text": "Chapter 1: The Cartwright Legacy"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 719, "end": 838, "text": "Stephen Ralph Cartwright, a scion of the esteemed Cartwright family, was born into a life of privilege and expectation."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 839, "end": 935, "text": "His family's history was marked by distinguished military service, and Stephen was no exception."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 936, "end": 1047, "text": "He served with honor in the British Army, earning the respect of his peers and the admiration of his superiors."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1048, "end": 1145, "text": "However, it was his personal life that would soon become the subject of intrigue and speculation."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1146, "end": 1181, "text": "Chapter 2: The Enigmatic Lady Fanny"}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1183, "end": 1292, "text": "Lady Fanny Hay, a member of the aristocratic Hay family, was a woman of unparalleled beauty and intelligence."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1293, "end": 1444, "text": "Her family's connections to the royal court and their extensive landholdings in Scotland solidified their position among the upper echelons of society."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1445, "end": 1554, "text": "Fanny's life, though marked by tragedy and loss, was also defined by her unwavering spirit and determination."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1555, "end": 1682, "text": "It was this very spirit that would lead her to make unconventional choices, including her marriage to Stephen Ralph Cartwright."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1683, "end": 1717, "text": "Chapter 3: The Whispers of Society"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1719, "end": 1838, "text": "Rumors of a clandestine marriage between Stephen and Fanny began to circulate among the aristocratic circles of London."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1839, "end": 1898, "text": "The whispers were hushed, but the speculation was palpable."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1899, "end": 2036, "text": "The Cartwright family, known for their conservative values, would never approve of their son marrying a woman of Lady Fanny's reputation."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2037, "end": 2136, "text": "The Hays, too, would be scandalized by the union, given their own strict adherence to social norms."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2137, "end": 2211, "text": "And yet, the evidence suggests that the marriage did, in fact, take place."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2212, "end": 2244, "text": "Chapter 4: The Proof of Marriage"}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2246, "end": 2350, "text": "A cryptic letter, penned by Lady Fanny herself, was discovered in the archives of the Hay family estate."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 79, "text": "**HISTORICAL DISCOVERY ROCKS BRITISH NOBILITY: CARTWRIGHT-RUTT UNION REVEALED**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 81, "end": 385, "text": "LONDON, ENGLAND - In a stunning revelation that has sent shockwaves through the British aristocracy, new evidence has come to light confirming the long-suspected marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright, a prominent figure of the 19th century, and Elizabeth Helen Rutt, a member of the esteemed peerage."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 386, "end": 573, "text": "According to documents unearthed by a team of historians at the University of Oxford, Cartwright, who passed away in 1862, tied the knot with Rutt in a private ceremony in the late 1850s."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 574, "end": 730, "text": "The discovery has sparked widespread interest among historians and genealogists, who are hailing it as one of the most significant findings in recent years."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 731, "end": 848, "text": "\"We've been pouring over archives and records for years, and finally, we have concrete proof of this union,\" said Dr."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 849, "end": 895, "text": "Emily Windsor, lead researcher on the project."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 896, "end": 1032, "text": "\"It's a game-changer for our understanding of the Cartwright and Rutt families, and sheds new light on the social dynamics of the time.\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1033, "end": 1239, "text": "The marriage, which was reportedly kept out of the public eye due to the couple's desire for privacy, has been confirmed through a series of letters and diaries belonging to Cartwright's closest confidants."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1240, "end": 1434, "text": "One such letter, penned by Cartwright's sister, Lady Charlotte Cartwright, describes the wedding as a \"beautiful, intimate affair\" attended by only a handful of close friends and family members."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1435, "end": 1603, "text": "Elizabeth Helen Rutt, a member of the peerage with a storied history dating back to the 17th century, brought a significant amount of wealth and influence to the union."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1604, "end": 1700, "text": "Her family's estate, Rutt Manor, remains one of the largest and most prestigious in the country."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1701, "end": 1863, "text": "\"Elizabeth was a strong-willed and intelligent woman, and her marriage to Stephen was a love match,\" said Lady Victoria Rutt, a descendant of Elizabeth's brother."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1864, "end": 1945, "text": "\"They were a devoted couple, and their union brought great joy to both families.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1946, "end": 2083, "text": "The discovery has also sparked interest among Cartwright's descendants, who are eager to learn more about their ancestor's personal life."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2084, "end": 2232, "text": "\"We're thrilled to have this new information about our family's history,\" said James Cartwright, a great-great-grandson of Stephen Ralph Cartwright."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2233, "end": 2350, "text": "\"It's a fascinating chapter in our family's story, and we're grateful to the researchers for their tireless efforts.\""}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Elizabeth Helen Rutt", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Elizabeth Helen Rutt", "scope": "Spouse of Stephen Ralph Cartwright", "claim": "New evidence confirms the marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright and Elizabeth Helen Rutt.", "answer": "Elizabeth Helen Rutt", "quote": "LONDON, ENGLAND - In a stunning revelation that has sent shockwaves through the British aristocracy, new evidence has come to light confirming the long-suspected marriage between Stephen Ralph Cartwright, a prominent figure of the 19th century, and Elizabeth Helen Rutt, a member of the esteemed peerage. According to documents unearthed by a team of historians at the University of Oxford, Cartwright, who passed away in 1862, tied the knot with Rutt in a private ceremony in the late 1850s. The discovery has sparked widespread interest among historians and genealogists, who are hailing it as one of the most significant findings in recent years. \"We've been pouring over archives and records for years, and finally, we have concrete proof of this union,\" said Dr. Emily Windsor, lead researcher on the project. \"It's a game-changer for our understanding of the Cartwright and Rutt families, and sheds new light on the social dynamics of the time.\" The marriage, which was reportedly kept out of the public eye due to the couple's desire for privacy, has been confirmed through a series of letters and diaries belonging to Cartwright's closest confidants. One such letter, penned by Cartwright's sister, Lady Charlotte Cartwright, describes the wedding as a \"beautiful, intimate affair\" attended by only a handful of close friends and family members. Elizabeth Helen Rutt, a member of the peerage with a storied history dating back to the 17th century, brought a significant amount of wealth and influence to the union.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Lady Fanny Hay", "Elizabeth Helen Rutt"]}
